course: dictionary
lesson: 8030
title: Refresh: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. Refresh is a good example. «A short nap of about 20 minutes early in the afternoon can refresh you.» Here refresh means to make you feel less tired and more lively again. Check it: could you put "wake you up and make you feel better" in its place? Yes, so that is the meaning.
explain: On a computer or phone, refresh means to load a page again so you see the newest version. «Ollie lay in bed refreshing it till midnight» means he kept reloading the page to see if anything new had appeared. The clues are the screen and the word page, so this is not about feeling lively.
explain: To refresh your memory means to remind yourself of something you have learned, like looking over your notes before a test. When you meet refresh, ask: is this about a tired body, a screen, or a memory? Then try that meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Refresh (verb) means to make someone feel less tired or hot, and more lively again.
fact: To refresh a web page or screen means to load it again so it shows the newest version.
fact: To refresh your memory means to remind yourself of something.
fact: A refresh (noun) is the act of reloading a page.
fact: «Refreshing» can describe something that makes you feel cool and lively, such as a refreshing drink on a hot day.
exercise: «A short nap of about 20 minutes early in the afternoon can refresh you.» What does refresh mean here? | *Make you feel less tired and more lively | Wash your face | Make you hot and sweaty | Put you to sleep for the whole night
exercise: «Ollie lay in bed refreshing it till midnight.» What is Ollie doing? | Writing a new message to his friends | Sleeping and dreaming | *Loading the page again and again to see new posts | Reading a library book
exercise: Mia says, "I need to refresh my memory before the spelling test." What does she mean? | She wants to wash her hair before the test | She wants to forget all the words | She wants a cold drink | *She wants to remind herself of the words she learned
test: Which meaning fits: «Broken sleep refreshes you less.»? | Makes you louder and more noisy | Makes you feel hungry | *Makes you feel less tired and more lively | Turns the lights off
test: "To refresh your memory" means what? | *Remind yourself of something | Clean the classroom | Buy a new bag | Forget something on purpose
exam: In «a refreshing drink on a hot day», what kind of word is refreshing? | *Adjective | Adverb | Verb | Noun
